                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for jianyu &amp;lt;yujian@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7c2f224e-8cb5-4ca6-8419-854431b8668f" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7c2f224e-8cb5-4ca6-8419-854431b8668f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_67 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Adding targets to pool
CMD: trevis-101vm6 /usr/sbin/lctl pool_add lustre.qpool1 lustre-OST[0000-0001/1]
trevis-101vm6: pool_add: lustre-OST0001_UUID is already in pool lustre.qpool1
CMD: trevis-101vm1 lctl get_param -n lov.lustre-*.pools.qpool1 |
			grep -e lustre-OST0000_UUID -e lustre-OST0001_UUID  | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ' 
Waiting 90s for 'lustre-OST0000_UUID lustre-OST0001_UUID '
CMD: trevis-101vm1 lctl get_param -n lov.lustre-*.pools.qpool1 |
			grep -e lustre-OST0000_UUID -e lustre-OST0001_UUID  | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ' 
CMD: trevis-101vm6 /usr/sbin/lctl get_param qmt.lustre-QMT0000.dt-qpool1.glb-usr
Granted 0 MB
 sanity-quota test_67: @@@@@@ FAIL: Granted(0) for quota_usr in qpool1 is wrong. 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;br/&gt;
clients: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4598" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4598&lt;/a&gt; - 6.4.0-150600.23.25-default&lt;br/&gt;
